{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-232500.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-232500.md'\"","aggregated_output":"Get-Content: \r\nLine |\r\n   2 |  Get-Content -Raw 'references/autonomous_design.md'; Get-Content -Raw  …\r\n     |  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n     | 找不到路径“D:\\project\\AdaRES_project\\references\\autonomous_design.md”，因为该路径不存在。\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 23:25 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Active 0/2 and candidate budget 2. S1 tested permutation equivariance; S2 tested localized appearance support in confidence selection.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nS1's fixed train64 averaging degraded mIoU 0.82256 to 0.80927. S2's inside versus outside perturbation showed local sensitivity, but the frozen top-two rule reached 0.82007 versus B4 0.82256 and outside control 0.82271. These are training-subset diagnostics, not validation results or evidence of full-run improvement.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo candidate passed diagnosis and controls. S1 and the specific S2 top-two rule are rejected. An S2 successor must specify a new causal information path and demonstrate paired improvement versus the outside-mask control before native backward/resources and implementation.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0/1 were idle at the one targeted pre-probe query (0%, 1 MiB). GPU0 read-only probes completed. Queue remains empty; no post-probe occupancy claim. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed 64-scene native S1/S2 read-only diagnosis and matched controls.\n- [x] Frozen selection interventions and raw evidence archived.\n- [ ] Future independent mechanism: paired training control, native backward and training resources, isolated model/config/tests.\n- [ ] No admission receipt, training sync, dispatch or queue update without all six hard gates.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nS1 order intervention exposes confidence sensitivity despite nearly unchanged masks. S2 perturbs mask quality and top-two is inferior to B4. Its 6.31 GiB inference peak is not training peak. No novelty claim.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nNo tuning-only, seed-repeat, pure ablation, banned or renamed-duplicate variant admitted. A score fusion or permutation-count scan would be tuning and is not proposed.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded cycle exhausted its two distinct tested routes, not global scientific exhaustion.\n\r\n# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 23:25 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020; B4-E30 0.5094; gap 0.0056. Goal constraints/bans checked: server-2 GPU0/1 only, one experiment per GPU, released backbone/project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, full metric/resource reporting, no validation scans.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Query competition | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target |\n| Equivariant confidence | Negative | S1 averaging 0.80927 vs B4 0.82256 on 64 training scenes | No selection benefit |\n| Local 2D support | Sensitivity, no admission | S2 inside/outside disruption and top-two 0.82007 vs B4 0.82256 | No control-beating selector |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. S1/S2 are native read-only probes, not trained experiments.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nSelected-versus-oracle headroom persists, but neither point-order consistency nor local 2D sensitivity supplies a reliable inference-time ranking. Active queries, full latency and training peak memory remain unmeasured for prior variants.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nS1 tested semantic-preserving representation stability against unchanged-repeat control. S2 tested local modality reliance against equal-count outside-mask and unchanged-repeat controls. Their frozen ranking interventions failed; further tuning of averaging, mask area, top-k or feature subsets is not justified.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-232500.md`; resume only on an independently justified metric-aligned confidence mechanism with all six hard gates.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -TotalCount 180 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_s2_local_appearance.py'; Get-Content -TotalCount 180 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_b4_selection.py'; Get-Content -TotalCount 180 'AdaRES/ipdn/model_paper5/adares_b4_query_competition/dec.py'\"","aggregated_output":"import argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport statistics\r\nimport sys\r\nimport types\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef predictor(self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\r\n              gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp):\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for index, target in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\r\n        valid = ~out[\"batch_mask\"][index]\r\n        masks = out[\"masks\"][index, :, valid].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\r\n        truth = target.gt(0.5).to(masks.device)\r\n        point_masks = masks[:, superpoints]\r\n        ious = (point_masks & truth).sum(-1).float() / (\r\n            (point_masks | truth).sum(-1).clamp_min(1).float()\r\n        )\r\n        scores = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], -1)[:, 1]\r\n        selected = int(scores.argmax())\r\n        top_two = scores.topk(2).indices.tolist()\r\n        changed = []\r\n        for variant, alternate in enumerate(self.alternates):\r\n            alt_masks = alternate[\"masks\"][index, :, valid].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\r\n            overlap = masks.float() @ alt_masks.float().T\r\n            union = (masks.sum(-1)[:, None] +\r\n                     alt_masks.sum(-1)[None, :] - overlap).clamp_min(1)\r\n            query = selected if variant < 3 else top_two[1]\r\n            base_seed = out[\"sample_inds\"][index, query]\r\n            same_seed = (alternate[\"sample_inds\"][index] == base_seed).nonzero(\r\n                as_tuple=True)[0]\r\n            match = (int(same_seed[0]) if same_seed.numel()\r\n                     else int((overlap / union)[query].argmax()))\r\n            alt_scores = F.softmax(alternate[\"indis\"][index], -1)[:, 1]\r\n            alt_point = alt_masks[:, superpoints]\r\n            alt_ious = (alt_point & truth).sum(-1).float() / (\r\n                (alt_point | truth).sum(-1).clamp_min(1).float()\r\n            )\r\n            changed.append({\r\n                \"selected_score_drop\": float(scores[query] - alt_scores[match]),\r\n                \"matched_score\": float(alt_scores[match]),\r\n                \"matched_mask_iou\": float((overlap / union)[query, match]),\r\n                \"selection_iou\": float(alt_ious[alt_scores.argmax()]),\r\n                \"selection_flip\": int(alt_scores.argmax()) != match,\r\n                \"same_seed\": bool(same_seed.numel()),\r\n            })\r\n        rows.append({\r\n            \"selected_iou\": float(ious[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_iou\": float(ious.max()),\r\n            \"selected_area\": int(masks[selected].sum()),\r\n            \"repeat\": changed[0],\r\n            \"inside\": changed[1],\r\n            \"outside\": changed[2],\r\n            \"runner_inside\": changed[3],\r\n            \"runner_outside\": changed[4],\r\n            \"top_two_inside_iou\": float(ious[\r\n                top_two[0] if changed[1][\"matched_score\"] >=\r\n                changed[3][\"matched_score\"] else top_two[1]]),\r\n            \"top_two_outside_iou\": float(ious[\r\n                top_two[0] if changed[2][\"matched_score\"] >=\r\n                changed[4][\"matched_score\"] else top_two[1]]),\r\n        })\r\n    return {\"rows\": rows}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=16)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=0)\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    data_cfg = cfg.data.train.copy()\r\n    data_cfg.training = False\r\n    data_cfg.aug = False\r\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\r\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, get_root_logger())\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint), strict=False)\r\n    allowed = {\"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\",\r\n               \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\"}\r\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    original = model.dec.forward\r\n\r\n    def intervened_forward(self, x, fps_seed_sp, batch_offsets,\r\n                           lang_feats=None, lang_masks=None, sp_pos=None,\r\n                           feats_2d=None):\r\n        base = original(x, fps_seed_sp, batch_offsets, lang_feats,\r\n                        lang_masks, sp_pos, feats_2d)\r\n        repeat = original(x, fps_seed_sp, batch_offsets, lang_feats,\r\n                          lang_masks, sp_pos, feats_2d)\r\n        lengths = (batch_offsets[1:] - batch_offsets[:-1]).tolist()\r\n        selected = base[\"indis\"].softmax(-1)[..., 1].argmax(-1)\r\n        alternatives = []\r\n        top_two = base[\"indis\"].softmax(-1)[..., 1].topk(2).indices\r\n        for rank in (0, 1):\r\n            for inside in (True, False):\r\n                changed = feats_2d.clone()\r\n                for index, (start, length) in enumerate(zip(\r\n                        batch_offsets[:-1].tolist(), lengths)):\r\n                    query = top_two[index, rank]\r\n                    mask = base[\"masks\"][index, query, :length].sigmoid() > 0.5\r\n                    on = mask.nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0]\r\n                    off = (~mask).nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0]\r\n                    count = min(on.numel(), off.numel())\r\n                    indices = (on if inside else off)[:count] + start\r\n                    if count > 1:\r\n                        changed[indices] = feats_2d[indices.roll(1)]\r\n                alternatives.append(original(\r\n                    x, fps_seed_sp, batch_offsets, lang_feats, lang_masks,\r\n                    sp_pos, changed,\r\n                ))\r\n        model.alternates = [repeat] + alternatives\r\n        return base\r\n\r\n    model.dec.forward = types.MethodType(intervened_forward, model.dec)\r\n    model.predict_by_feat = types.MethodType(predictor, model)\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for scene in range(min(args.scenes, len(dataset))):\r\n        with torch.no_grad():\r\n            rows.extend(model(dataset.collate_fn([dataset[scene]]),\r\n                              mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"])\r\n    errors = [r for r in rows if r[\"oracle_iou\"] - r[\"selected_iou\"] > 0.05]\r\n    result = {\r\n        \"scenes\": min(args.scenes, len(dataset)),\r\n        \"expressions\": len(rows),\r\n        \"material_errors\": len(errors),\r\n        \"indicator_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"inside_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"inside\"][\"selection_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"outside_miou\": statistics.fmean(r[\"outside\"][\"selection_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"inside_flips\": sum(r[\"inside\"][\"selection_flip\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"outside_flips\": sum(r[\"outside\"][\"selection_flip\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"error_inside_greater_drop\": sum(\r\n            r[\"inside\"][\"selected_score_drop\"] >\r\n            r[\"outside\"][\"selected_score_drop\"] for r in errors),\r\n        \"all_inside_greater_drop\": sum(\r\n            r[\"inside\"][\"selected_score_drop\"] >\r\n            r[\"outside\"][\"selected_score_drop\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"inside_mask_iou\": statistics.fmean(\r\n            r[\"inside\"][\"matched_mask_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"outside_mask_iou\": statistics.fmean(\r\n            r[\"outside\"][\"matched_mask_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"repeat_mismatch\": sum(\r\n            abs(r[\"repeat\"][\"selected_score_drop\"]) > 1e-4\r\n            or r[\"repeat\"][\"matched_mask_iou\"] < 0.9999 for r in rows),\r\n        \"repeat_miou\": statistics.fmean(\r\n            r[\"repeat\"][\"selection_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"inside_same_seed\": sum(r[\"inside\"][\"same_seed\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"outside_same_seed\": sum(r[\"outside\"][\"same_seed\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"runner_inside_same_seed\": sum(\r\n            r[\"runner_inside\"][\"same_seed\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"top_two_inside_miou\": statistics.fmean(\r\n            r[\"top_two_inside_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"top_two_outside_miou\": statistics.fmean(\r\n            r[\"top_two_outside_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"top_two_inside_flips\": sum(\r\n            r[\"top_two_inside_iou\"] != r[\"selected_iou\"] for r in rows),\r\n        \"peak_reserved_gib\": torch.cuda.max_memory_reserved() / 2**30,\r\n        \"rows\": rows,\r\n    }\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport statistics\r\nimport sys\r\nimport types\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef selection_predictor():\r\n    def predict_by_feat(\r\n        self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\r\n        gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp,\r\n    ):\r\n        rows = []\r\n        for index, target in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\r\n            masks = out[\"masks\"][index].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\r\n            scores = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], dim=-1)[:, 1]\r\n            selected = int(scores.argmax())\r\n            point_masks = masks[:, superpoints]\r\n            truth = target.gt(0.5).to(point_masks.device)\r\n            intersection = (point_masks & truth).sum(-1).float()\r\n            union = (point_masks | truth).sum(-1).float()\r\n            ious = intersection / union.clamp_min(1)\r\n            oracle = int(ious.argmax())\r\n            pair_intersection = (masks[selected] & masks[oracle]).sum().float()\r\n            pair_union = (masks[selected] | masks[oracle]).sum().float()\r\n            rows.append({\r\n                \"selected_iou\": float(ious[selected]),\r\n                \"oracle_iou\": float(ious[oracle]),\r\n                \"selected_oracle_overlap\": float(\r\n                    pair_intersection / pair_union.clamp_min(1)\r\n                ),\r\n                \"oracle_score_rank\": int(\r\n                    (scores.argsort(descending=True) == oracle)\r\n                    .nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0].item()\r\n                ) + 1,\r\n                \"selected_query\": selected,\r\n                \"oracle_query\": oracle,\r\n            })\r\n        return {\"rows\": rows}\r\n\r\n    return predict_by_feat\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=16)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--model\",\r\n        choices=(\"adares_b4_query_competition\", \"adares_g1_metric_targets\"),\r\n        default=\"adares_b4_query_competition\",\r\n    )\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n\r\n    if args.model == \"adares_g1_metric_targets\":\r\n        from ipdn.model_paper5.adares_g1_metric_targets import IPDN\r\n    else:\r\n        from ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\n\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    data_cfg = cfg.data.val.copy()\r\n    data_cfg.training = False\r\n    data_cfg.aug = False\r\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\r\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\r\n    logger = get_root_logger()\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, logger)\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    state = checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint)\r\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(state, strict=False)\r\n    allowed = {\r\n        \"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\",\r\n        \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\",\r\n    }\r\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\r\n    model.predict_by_feat = types.MethodType(selection_predictor(), model)\r\n\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for index in range(min(args.scenes, len(dataset))):\r\n        batch = dataset.collate_fn([dataset[index]])\r\n        with torch.no_grad():\r\n            rows.extend(model(batch, mode=\"predict\")[\"rows\"])\r\n    if not rows:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(\"No expressions in diagnostic subset\")\r\n    errors = [row for row in rows if row[\"oracle_iou\"] - row[\"selected_iou\"] > 0.05]\r\n    result = {\r\n        \"checkpoint\": args.checkpoint,\r\n        \"scenes\": min(args.scenes, len(dataset)),\r\n        \"expressions\": len(rows),\r\n        \"top1_miou\": statistics.fmean(row[\"selected_iou\"] for row in rows),\r\n        \"oracle_miou\": statistics.fmean(row[\"oracle_iou\"] for row in rows),\r\n        \"material_error_count\": len(errors),\r\n        \"error_pair_overlap_mean\": (\r\n            statistics.fmean(row[\"selected_oracle_overlap\"] for row in errors)\r\n            if errors else None\r\n        ),\r\n        \"error_pair_overlap_ge_half\": sum(\r\n            row[\"selected_oracle_overlap\"] >= 0.5 for row in errors\r\n        ),\r\n        \"error_oracle_rank_le_three\": sum(\r\n            row[\"oracle_score_rank\"] <= 3 for row in errors\r\n        ),\r\n        \"rows\": rows,\r\n    }\r\n    Path(args.output).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n    print(json.dumps({key: value for key, value in result.items() if key != \"rows\"}))\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn as nn\r\nfrom .sample_model import SamplingModule\r\nimport ipdn.torch.nn_new.functional as F\r\nfrom ipdn.torch.nn_new import MultiheadAttention\r\n\r\nclass ThreeLayerMLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"A 3-layer MLP with normalization and dropout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, dim, out_dim):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, dim, 1, bias=False),\r\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(dim),\r\n            nn.ReLU(),\r\n            nn.Dropout(0.3),\r\n            nn.Conv1d(dim, out_dim, 1)\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        \"\"\"Forward pass, x can be (B, dim, N).\"\"\"\r\n        return self.net(x)\r\n\r\nclass CrossAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(d_model, nhead, dropout=dropout, batch_first=True)\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self._reset_parameters()\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n\r\n    def _reset_parameters(self):\r\n        for p in self.parameters():\r\n            if p.dim() > 1:\r\n                nn.init.xavier_uniform_(p)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, source, query, batch_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        source (B, N_p, d_model)\r\n        batch_offsets Tensor (b, n_p)\r\n        query Tensor (b, n_q, d_model)\r\n        attn_masks Tensor (b, n_q, n_p)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = query.shape[0]\r\n        query = self.with_pos_embed(query, pe)\r\n        k = v = source\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, query.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(query, k, v, key_padding_mask=batch_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        self.dropout(output)\r\n        output = output + query\r\n        self.norm(output)\r\n\r\n        return output, output_weight, src_weight # (b, n_q, d_model), (b, n_q, n_v)\r\n\r\nclass SelfAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model=256, nhead=8, dropout=0.0, glu = False):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.attn = MultiheadAttention(\r\n            d_model,\r\n            nhead,\r\n            dropout=dropout,\r\n            batch_first=True,\r\n        )\r\n        self.nhead = nhead\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\r\n        self.glu = glu\r\n        if glu:\r\n            self.glu_p = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n            self.glu_g = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)\r\n\r\n    def with_pos_embed(self, tensor, pos):\r\n        return tensor if pos is None else tensor + pos\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, x_mask=None, attn_mask=None, pe=None, norm=True, att_weights=None):\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        x Tensor (b, n_w, c)\r\n        x_mask Tensor (b, n_w)\r\n        \"\"\"\r\n        B = x.shape[0]\r\n        q = k = self.with_pos_embed(x, pe)\r\n        if attn_mask is not None:\r\n            attn_mask = attn_mask.unsqueeze(1).repeat(1, self.nhead, 1, 1).view(B*self.nhead, q.shape[1], k.shape[1])\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, attn_mask=attn_mask, att_weights =att_weights)  # (1, 100, d_model)\r\n        else:\r\n            output, output_weight, src_weight = self.attn(q, k, x, key_padding_mask=x_mask, att_weights =att_weights)\r\n        if self.glu:\r\n            output = self.glu_p(output) * (self.glu_g(output).sigmoid())\r\n        output = self.dropout(output) + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass FFN(nn.Module):\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model, hidden_dim, dropout=0.0, activation_fn='relu'):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        if activation_fn == 'relu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.ReLU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        elif activation_fn == 'gelu':\r\n            self.net = nn.Sequential(\r\n                nn.Linear(d_model, hidden_dim),\r\n                nn.GELU(),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n                nn.Linear(hidden_dim, d_model),\r\n                nn.Dropout(dropout),\r\n            )\r\n        self.norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x, norm=True):\r\n        output = self.net(x)\r\n        output = output + x\r\n        if norm: output = self.norm(output)\r\n        return output\r\n\r\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\" Very simple multi-layer perceptron (also called FFN)\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, hidden_dim, output_dim, num_layers):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.num_layers = num_layers\r\n        h = [hidden_dim] * (num_layers - 1)\r\n        self.layers = nn.ModuleList(nn.Linear(n, k) for n, k in zip([input_dim] + h, h + [output_dim]))\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, x):\r\n        for i, layer in enumerate(self.layers):\r\n            x = F.relu(layer(x)) if i < self.num_layers - 1 else layer(x)\r\n        return x\r\n\r\n\r\nclass QueryCompetitionIndicator(nn.Module):\r\n    \"\"\"Predict confidence from a query and its overlapping competitors.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, d_model):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.query_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model)\r\n        self.evidence_norm = nn.LayerNorm(3 * d_model + 1)\r\n        self.head = nn.Sequential(\r\n            nn.Linear(3 * d_model + 1, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, d_model),\r\n            nn.GELU(),\r\n            nn.Linear(d_model, 2),\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    def forward(self, query, pred_masks, batch_mask):\r\n        valid = (~batch_mask).unsqueeze(1).to(pred_masks.dtype)\r\n        probabilities = pred_masks.sigmoid() * valid\r\n        areas = probabilities.sum(-1)\r\n        intersection = torch.einsum(\r\n            'bim,bjm->bij', probabilities, probabilities\r\n        )\r\n        union = areas.unsqueeze(-1) + areas.unsqueeze(1) - intersection\r\n        overlap = intersection / union.clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        diagonal = torch.eye(\r\n            overlap.shape[-1], dtype=torch.bool, device=overlap.device\r\n        ).unsqueeze(0)\r\n        overlap = overlap.masked_fill(diagonal, 0.0)\r\n\r\n        competition = overlap / overlap.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)\r\n        normalized_query = self.query_norm(query)\r\n        context = torch.einsum('bij,bjd->bid', competition, normalized_query)\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
