{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/decisions/20260926-220404_route_change.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/decisions/20260926-211359_route_change.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-R1-R2_diagnosis_20260926-220200.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-Q1-Q2_diagnosis_20260926-210900.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 22:04:04\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: R1/R2 fixed native training diagnoses: admit either of two vacant server-2 slots?\n- **决策**: Reject oracle-positive filtering R1 and frozen peer-confidence R2; leave server-2 GPU0/1 unqueued\n- **依据**: R1 positive-restricted oracle 0.8920 uses unavailable labels and G1/C1 already failed; R2 product 0.7961 vs B4 0.8225 with 30 strict repeat mismatches\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-R1-R2_diagnosis_20260926-220200.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-26 21:13:58\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: Q1/Q2 native training diagnoses: admit either vacant server-2 GPU slot?\n- **决策**: Reject Q1 token-attention concentration and Q2 attention-mask support; leave GPU0/1 unqueued\n- **依据**: Q1 annotated-target attention advantage weak against rotated control, concentration-only mIoU 0.08395 vs 0.82256; Q2 oracle support higher in only 70/388 errors; diagnosis/controls gates unmet\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-Q1-Q2_diagnosis_20260926-210900.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Native diagnostic cycle: R1 and R2\n\n2026-09-26 22:02 Asia/Shanghai. Prepared preflight used once. Server-2 GPU0 key SSH, fixed first 64 ScanRefer training scenes, 1660 expressions, B4-E30 best checkpoint; no training or queue mutation. R1/R2 are inference-only diagnostics and cannot establish validation efficacy.\n\n## R1: Matched-positive supervision versus final mask quality\n\nReconstructed standard positive assignments from training instance labels and sampled seeds, with a nearest-center fallback. Among 388 material errors (oracle IoU minus selected IoU > 0.05), 179 selected queries were labeled positive while the oracle was negative; 83 had the reverse, 80 had both positive, 46 both negative. Standard positive queries comprise 4.53% of queries. Selected/oracle/positive-restricted oracle mean IoU: 0.82256/0.91035/0.89203. Constraining the *existing* B4 score to oracle positive labels would yield 0.87880, but those labels are not available at inference. Repeated forwards produced zero readout mismatches in the final run. This documents supervision headroom, not an admissible positive-filter method. G1 directly replaced indicator targets with detached mask IoU and finished at 0.4980 versus B4-E30 0.5094; C1 listwise indicator finished at 0.5008. Do not rename or rerun either route.\n\n## R2: Overlap-weighted peer confidence\n\nPredeclared directed peer confidence was soft-mask-IoU-weighted mean of *other* queries' B4 probabilities. Controls: one-query cyclic rotation of the same peer probabilities; unweighted overlap degree. The missed oracle had greater directed peer support in 287/387 material errors versus 198/387 rotated peers and 102/387 plain overlaps. On the same 1660 examples, support-only mIoU was 0.78019; frozen confidence times peer support was 0.79612, versus B4 0.82254. Rotated and plain products reached 0.72816 and 0.79839, respectively. Product flipped 650 selections. The repeated native pass had 30 readout mismatches at the strict 1e-4 threshold, and 387 rather than 388 material errors; the weaker direction cannot support admission. This specific propagation rule is rejected. The first pass was directionally similar (288/388) but was superseded by the product probe.\n\n## Gates and next action\n\nR1 is an observational ceiling, not a proposed executable mechanism: oracle-positive filtering is label leakage, and direct metric targets/listwise alternatives G1/C1 already failed. Reject positive-filtering as a candidate; reopen only upon independent inference-available evidence for a distinct mechanism, not a rename of G1/C1 or a validation proxy scan. R2 fails the frozen diagnosis/control intervention. Neither passes native backward or training-resource gates; no admission receipt, sync, dispatch or training launch. The 3.48 GiB R2 inference peak is not training peak. No global hypothesis exhaustion claim.\n\r\n# Native diagnostic cycle: Q1 and Q2\n\n2026-09-26 21:09 Asia/Shanghai. Prepared monitor/goal preflight used once. Server-2 GPU0, key SSH, B4-E30 best checkpoint, fixed first 64 training scenes (1660 expressions). Read-only native inference; no training or queue mutation. Both probes repeated each forward. Scene 16-63 is a disjoint within-training check, not validation efficacy.\n\n## Q1: Query-to-token attention\n\nThe final query-to-language attention map is computed in B4 but not supplied directly to its competition indicator. Predeclared concentration statistic was squared attention mass summed over valid tokens. In 388 material selection errors, the missed oracle was more concentrated in 260, mean 0.06480 versus selected 0.06173. Concentration-only selection was poor: mIoU 0.08395 versus B4 0.82256. On scenes 16-63, the direction persisted in 186/281 errors, but the attention mass on annotated target tokens favored the oracle in only 147/281; a one-position rotated-token null favored it in 115/281. Full 64-scene target-token counts were 206/388 versus rotated null 160/388. This is a weak, nonspecific signal; positive-map annotations are training-only and cannot be used as inference inputs. The initial exact repeat on 16 scenes differed by 3.7e-8, below the corrected numerical tolerance. On 64 scenes two repeated readouts exceeded 1e-5, maximum 8.67e-5, so strict numerical determinism is not claimed. No attention-feature/fusion-weight scan.\n\n## Q2: Query-to-scene attention support\n\nThe final coarse query-to-scene attention map was paired with both the final predicted mask and the previous-layer mask that constrained attention. In 388 material errors, oracle support exceeded selected support in only 70 using the final mask and 25 using the previous mask. Mean final support was 0.91037 oracle versus 0.96527 selected; support-only mIoU 0.55651 versus B4 0.82256. This disconfirms the predicted direction, and previous-mask dependence further weakens an independent evidence claim. One repeated support value exceeded the 1e-4 tolerance despite a maximum reported selected/oracle deviation of 2.86e-6; this implies a discrete selection/oracle mismatch and needs no rescue by tuning.\n\n## Gates and disposition\n\nQ1 has a directional observation but fails a convincing metric-aligned, inference-valid matched-control diagnosis; an annotation-conditioned attention target would leak training supervision into the proposed inference claim. Q2 is directionally disconfirmed. Both are independent from the earlier pooled-mask/text J1 and topology P1 mechanisms, but neither passes diagnosis and controls. Native backward, candidate-specific training resources, independent model implementation, admission receipt, sync and dispatch were not attempted. The inference peak reserved memory was 3.48 GiB (Q1) and 3.56 GiB (Q2), not training peak. Reject both specific routes; no claim of global hypothesis exhaustion.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
